lass=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, Pike County&rsquo;s record runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025 across 8 grids. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids, August to September and September to October each came in under 90% of normal in 36 years. In 2025 November to December came in at 54% of normal on the middle, and in 2026 so far January to February and February to March each sat at 57%. Grid 17245 had its driest year in 1963 at 58% of normal.</p>"}
